findings.suggestion:
Put the child in its own process group (add "syscall" to the imports) so group-wide signals sent to the hub do not kill the workbench:

	cmd.SysProcAttr = &syscall.SysProcAttr{Setpgid: true}

then start it as usual.

Capture and log the Wait error (add "log" to the imports). If the caller should learn about early failures, you could also wait briefly for a quick exit and surface it, but at minimum record it:

	go func() {
		if waitErr := cmd.Wait(); waitErr != nil {
			log.Printf("automation workbench exited: %v", waitErr)
		}
	}()

fix.after:
go func() {
	if waitErr := cmd.Wait(); waitErr != nil {
		log.Printf("automation workbench exited: %v", waitErr)
	}
}()

